WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.770
Making movies is dangerous business, and making
exciting movies can be downright deadly.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:08.510
It's not all special effects — there's real
danger that goes along with all of that big

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:09.519
screen magic.

00:00:09.519 --> 00:00:13.419
Here's a look at a few famous movie scenes
that nearly killed actors.

00:00:13.419 --> 00:00:14.679
Daniel Day-Lewis

00:00:14.679 --> 00:00:18.839
Despite Daniel Day-Lewis's habit of putting
himself in danger for his roles, no stunts

00:00:18.839 --> 00:00:22.500
were as dangerous as the pneumonia the actor
contracted on the set of Gangs of New York

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.670
after refusing to wear anything other than
his ragged 19th-century wardrobe coat, despite

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:28.130
frigid temperatures.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:31.929
He also apparently fought random strangers
while filming in Rome just to keep in character

00:00:31.929 --> 00:00:35.050
as the violent Bill the Butcher, who he described
to The Independent as,

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:39.030
"...a bit of a punk, a marvellous character
and a joy to be — but not so good for my

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:40.530
physical or mental health."

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:46.200
"A joy to be" is an interesting way to describe
getting your butt kicked by Italian randos.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.430
But then again, we're talking about a guy
who spent three years getting punched in the

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:53.560
head to prepare for The Boxer by former champ
Barry McGuigan, so maybe everything he says

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:55.829
isn't going to make the most sense.

00:00:55.829 --> 00:00:59.769
"I drink your milkshake!

00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:01.829
Slllrrrppppp!"

00:01:01.829 --> 00:01:03.250
Jennifer Lawrence

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:07.610
Accident-prone Jennifer Lawrence has a habit
of taking public spills, but it was no laughing

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:11.200
matter when a smoke machine malfunctioned
and almost suffocated her on the set of The

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.720
Hunger Games: Mockingjay – Part 1.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:15.040
According to an insider on the set,

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:19.040
"Filming came to an abrupt halt when this
fog machine broke and began spewing so much

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:22.960
dense smoke during a tunnel sequence that
Jennifer literally disappeared from sight."

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:27.280
Luckily, she escaped with only a bit of vertigo
and nausea, but this wasn't the only time

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:29.470
The Hunger Games series knocked her around.

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:33.070
During training, she ran into a wall, sparking
rumors that she had damaged her spleen...

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.280
"Oh sorry, spleen juice."

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:40.710
...which turned out to be false.

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:45.000
But the next time everyone freaks out when
Lawrence asks to be paid the same as her male

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.480
costars, maybe we should all remember that
she's willing to bleed for our entertainment.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:50.880
Joseph Gordon-Levitt

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:55.830
After safely starring in a Batman movie, a
time-traveling assassin movie, and a G.I.

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:59.570
Joe movie, Joseph Gordon-Levitt was almost
killed…while playing a bike messenger.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:04.240
While 30 miles per hour might not sound too
fast, cruising between moving cars at that

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:05.950
speed on a bike is pretty serious.

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:10.670
A taxi drove over safety cones during filming
of Premium Rush and cut Gordon-Levitt off,

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:13.799
sending him through the rear windshield and
badly slicing up his forearm.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.700
"Joe got the award for most stitches with
31 when he went through the back window of

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:19.700
a cab."

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:24.930
"It's funny how much attention you'll get
when there's some blood involved."

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:28.610
"This is Joe's bike, and that's where he ended
up."

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:31.019
Director David Koepp feared he was dead, and
later told MTV,

00:02:31.019 --> 00:02:35.390
"And you're, ya know, for about 15 seconds
before I could get there and see what happened.

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:37.519
I'm thinking 'Did I kill him?

00:02:37.519 --> 00:02:39.549
Did I actually kill an actor?'"

00:02:39.549 --> 00:02:43.310
Gordon-Levitt actually laughed the whole thing
off, but we wonder if he thought it was so

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:47.450
funny when the movie's worldwide gross came
in $4 million below the production budget?

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:48.560
"Aah!"

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:51.420
"Aaaaahhhh!"

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:53.069
Jackie Chan

00:02:53.069 --> 00:02:57.700
The list of Jackie Chan's endless on-set injuries
is basically a medical encyclopedia of busted

00:02:57.700 --> 00:02:59.000
up body parts.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:02.359
But his injury on the set of Armour of God
II was the worst of all.

00:03:02.359 --> 00:03:05.340
Compared to some of the stuff he's done — like
sliding down the side of a skyscraper, and

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:08.640
getting hit by a real, flying helicopter — the
Armour of God II stunt was tame.

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:12.689
All he had to do was jump into a tree, but
he missed and fell to the ground, smacking

00:03:12.689 --> 00:03:15.620
his head on a rock, which sent a piece of
his skull into his brain.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:19.420
The injury required brain surgery, and a metal
plate implanted in Chan's skull.

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:23.810
Amazingly, this happened in the early '90s,
and Chan continued to make many more films,

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:25.950
performing almost all of his own stunts.

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:29.279
In other words, the exact opposite of what
any normal person would do.

00:03:29.279 --> 00:03:31.409
But then, Jackie Chan isn't a normal person.

00:03:31.409 --> 00:03:34.480
"I wanna be a Brontosaurus.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.709
Agh difficult!"

00:03:35.709 --> 00:03:36.700
Donald Sutherland

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:39.840
Most of the people on this list were badly
injured — and yes, could have been killed

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:43.290
in their on-set accidents — but none went
through quite the nightmare Donald Sutherland

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:44.290
endured.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.290
Because he actually died.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:50.709
On the set of Kelly's Heroes in 1968, Sutherland
contracted bacterial meningitis from the Danube

00:03:50.709 --> 00:03:52.939
River and had an out-of-body experience.

00:03:52.939 --> 00:03:54.959
His description of the incident is truly chilling.

00:03:54.959 --> 00:03:57.200
"The downward journey slowed and stopped.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.260
I'd been on my way to being dead when some
memory of the desperate rigor I'd applied

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:02.970
to survive all my childhood illnesses pulled
me back.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:04.069
Forced me to live.

00:04:04.069 --> 00:04:05.069
I was alive.

00:04:05.069 --> 00:04:06.189
I'd come out of the coma.

00:04:06.189 --> 00:04:07.700
Sick as a dog, but alive."

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:10.370
Both poetic and terrifying all at once.

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:13.859
Sutherland took over six weeks to recover,
at which point his contract forced him back

00:04:13.859 --> 00:04:17.650
on screen, with his brain still fried, afraid
of water and heights, and — according to

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:19.050
him -- constantly weeping.

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:22.380
"Don't hit me with them negative waves so
early in the morning."

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.940
Jason Statham

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:27.760
Action star Jason Statham knew exactly what
to expect when Sylvester Stallone asked him

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:32.010
back for The Expendables 3...except for the
fact that he'd almost get drowned, blown up,

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:35.430
or crushed to death — whichever one of those
happens when you accidentally drive a truck

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:36.900
off a loading dock.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:40.630
Something went wrong with the brakes in Statham's
vehicle, causing the truck to quickly plunge

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:41.630
60 feet.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:45.130
But Statham, who once competed as an Olympic
diver, was able to get free.

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:48.930
"The survival sort of kicks in and you pull
yourself out of the window and you start grabbing

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:50.470
at the water and trying to get to the surface."

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:50.990
"Could you see anything?

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:51.710
Was it dark?"

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:53.570
"Ya, I mean they don't call it the Black Sea
for no reason."

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:55.060
Apparently, Sly was unconcerned.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:59.400
"I look out and I say 'Where's Sly?' and he's,
ya know, stood on the side of dock there with

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:03.970
his iPhone, like that going 'Eh uh Jason,
ya need a towel?'"

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:04.970
"Hahaha"

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:05.970
Thanks for watching!

